- No concrete skill names in the synthetic fields.
- No skill-specific example words or mode/state words in the synthetic fields.
- No skill block, XML, angle-bracket tag, or code fence in the synthetic fields.
- No markdown, bullets, lists, or extra sentences in the synthetic fields.
- `synth_content` ends by forcing only the requested confirmation.
- `synth_reasoning` ends by committing to answer only with the requested confirmation.
- The pair is generic enough to sit before any future real skill activation.
